    "customfield_12313320": "<div style='font-weight:bold;color:red;text-align:center'>This project has a <a href=\"https://lucene.apache.org/core/discussion.html\">user mailing list and an IRC channel</a> for support. If you are looking for support, or if you are not sure whether the behavior that you are observing is expected or not, please discuss it there first.</div>",
    "customfield_12314134": null,
    "duedate": null,
    "customfield_12314132": null,
    "customfield_12314131": null,
    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12529818/comment/13142024",
          "id": "13142024",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=dafna",
            "name": "dafna",
            "key": "dafna",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Dafna Sheinwald",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Hi Shai,\nI would vote for (2). We may want to still maintain the option to implement both in one Lucene index, in order to avoid the burden of synch-ing them. \nRegards, Dafna.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=dafna",
            "name": "dafna",
            "key": "dafna",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Dafna Sheinwald",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2011-11-02T09:34:04.979+0000",
          "updated": "2011-11-02T09:34:04.979+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12529818/comment/13142031",
          "id": "13142031",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "body": "What do you mean? If we'll combine the search and taxonomy index, I don't believe we'll call it TaxonomyWriter. The purpose of the interface is for allowing a different implementation of the taxonomy, i.e. something that is not based on a Lucene Directory (e.g. a DB or something).\n\nPerhaps I misunderstand you?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "created": "2011-11-02T09:47:28.337+0000",
          "updated": "2011-11-02T09:47:28.337+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12529818/comment/13142082",
          "id": "13142082",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=dafna",
            "name": "dafna",
            "key": "dafna",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Dafna Sheinwald",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Hi Shai,\nYes, the old (already forgotten) DB implementation of taxonomy index, and the subsequent Lucene implementation gave rise to the definition of TaxonomyReader/Writer interface. Currently, indeed, and we are left with Lucene (Directory) implementation only. But I thought that as the interface is already there, and we have some thoughts of yet another implementation of taxonomy index (and hence TaxonomyReader/Writer), as part of the Lucene search index, which may help to ease the burden of synch between these two indices, why not let the interface live a bit longer before we remove it.   Regards, Dafna.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=dafna",
            "name": "dafna",
            "key": "dafna",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Dafna Sheinwald",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2011-11-02T12:18:08.552+0000",
          "updated": "2011-11-02T12:18:08.552+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12529818/comment/13142108",
          "id": "13142108",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "body": "Ok, let's keep the interface. It's harmful and I can certainly think of alternate taxonomy implementations. Perhaps one day someone would want to implement the taxonomy over a serialized FST or some other data structure ...\n\nSo in this case, I'll:\n* Keep the interfaces\n* Make TaxomomyWriter extend TwoPhaseCommit\n* Rename Lucene TaxoWriter/Reader to DirectoryTaxoWriterReader.\n\nAny suggestions about an alternative names to the implementations?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
